{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03345",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.9,
      "end_seconds": 4.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.92,
      "end_seconds": 8.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.67,
      "end_seconds": 15.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "It's shaking. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.44,
      "end_seconds": 17.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.07,
      "end_seconds": 25.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "One week, I think... sorry, about two weeks, I got that wrong."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.18,
      "end_seconds": 37.2,
      "duration_seconds": 11.02,
      "text": "Okay, go on. Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.71,
      "end_seconds": 48.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.92,
      "text": "I'd say a couple of times a week. A eight out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.58,
      "end_seconds": 55.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Have you been feeling anxious and agitated?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.67,
      "end_seconds": 66.02,
      "duration_seconds": 9.35,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, two months. About feeling anxious and agitated, it feels severe to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 83.56,
      "end_seconds": 92.67,
      "duration_seconds": 9.11,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Respiratory rate 16, heart rate 112. BP is 123 over 74, SpO2 97 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.15,
      "end_seconds": 95.13,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.33,
      "end_seconds": 100.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.71,
      "end_seconds": 103.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.92,
      "end_seconds": 107.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.86,
      "end_seconds": 122.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "You have a coarse tremor, a fast pulse and you are sweating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.67,
      "end_seconds": 129.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.65,
      "end_seconds": 145.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Any vomiting blood, seeing things or seizure?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.29,
      "end_seconds": 149.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.77,
      "end_seconds": 152.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "How about confusion?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.59,
      "end_seconds": 157.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Okay, so I haven't noticed any confusion."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.69,
      "end_seconds": 164.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.9,
      "end_seconds": 168.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.74,
      "end_seconds": 173.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "So, has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.88,
      "end_seconds": 180.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "I've had asthma for five years now. I have diabetes, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.68,
      "end_seconds": 186.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.85,
      "end_seconds": 197.8,
      "duration_seconds": 9.95,
      "text": "I had a reaction to amoxicillin when I was younger, a rash all over, and I've avoided it since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.05,
      "end_seconds": 203.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.12,
      "end_seconds": 215.81,
      "duration_seconds": 11.69,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years. Not much, I mostly stay in these days. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.92,
      "end_seconds": 220.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.1,
      "end_seconds": 228.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "It's Asthalin inhaler, when needed. Glimepiride. I take it 2 milligrams, before breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.47,
      "end_seconds": 232.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "So, since when have you been taking it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.95,
      "end_seconds": 235.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "About two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.05,
      "end_seconds": 255.62,
      "duration_seconds": 8.57,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: This looks most like alcohol withdrawal. Another possibility is an anxiety state."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.93,
      "end_seconds": 259.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.9,
      "end_seconds": 293.97,
      "duration_seconds": 34.07,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's alcohol withdrawal, and we'll know more once the blood tests is back. I'd like to arrange blood tests for alcohol withdrawal. For this, chlordiazepoxide, 20 milligrams, four times a day, reducing over five days. That's for alcohol withdrawal. The treatment will be thiamine, 100 milligrams, three times a day, long term. It's for alcohol-related deficiency. Do not stop alcohol suddenly without medical support."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.2,
      "end_seconds": 301.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "I'd like you to see the alcohol liaison service as well, and I'll write the referral."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.95,
      "end_seconds": 309.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Sure, uh, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.31,
      "end_seconds": 320.15,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "Please don't wait if the symptoms get worse. That's when to be seen urgently. See me again in two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.0,
      "end_seconds": 323.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Erm, alright, I'll be back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.9,
      "end_seconds": 329.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.01,
      "end_seconds": 333.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}